# Copy to .env — .env is gitignored and must stay that way.
#
# The custody mnemonic for your THROWAWAY test account.
# Never put a mnemonic you care about here, and never copy this file
# to the read-node server. Key issuance runs on your local machine only.
TEST_MNEMONIC=

# Filled in after registration, for convenience.
TEST_FID=
TEST_CUSTODY_ADDRESS=

# Public Optimism RPC — no API key required.
OP_RPC_URL=https://mainnet.optimism.io

# --- Provider -------------------------------------------------------------
# Default is AWS, configured with `aws configure` rather than through this file.
# AWS is the default because Hetzner Cloud caps new accounts at 1024 GB of volume
# storage, which is not enough to complete a Snapchain restore (peak ~1,580 GB).
#
# SNAPSTART_PROVIDER=hetzner
# SNAPSTART_AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# SNAPSTART_DISK_GB=2048

# Hetzner Cloud API token. Only needed when SNAPSTART_PROVIDER=hetzner.
#
# Scope it to a dedicated, otherwise-empty Hetzner project: this token can create
# and destroy servers and volumes in whatever project issued it, so a blast radius
# of "one empty project" is worth the thirty seconds it takes to make one.
#
# The read node itself never sees this token and needs no credentials of any kind
# once it is running.
#
# The CLI does still need it for `status` and `destroy`, which query and delete
# cloud resources. Keep it until you have destroyed the server, or delete it now
# and issue a fresh one when you tear down.
HETZNER_TOKEN=
